From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] udfread: accept a metadata file stored as a File Entry

A UDF 2.50 volume keeps its directories in a metadata partition, whose
location comes from the metadata file (and its mirror). The library only
accepted that file as an Extended File Entry (tag 266) and gave up on any
other tag, so a volume whose metadata file is a plain File Entry (tag 261)
could not be mounted at all.

Such images exist. On them every
lookup failed, so Kodi did not see BDMV/index.bdmv, took it for a DVD and
failed to open it; libbluray reads it through the same library.

Ordinary files and directories are already read from either tag. The
metadata file is now decoded the same way; the checks that follow (file
type, allocation) are unchanged. With this the image lists in full (178
entries, index.bdmv included), and an image that already worked lists
byte for byte the same.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/src/udfread.c
+++ b/src/udfread.c
@@ -526,12 +526,14 @@
             tag_id = _read_descriptor_block(input, pd->start_block + mirror_lba, buf);
         }
 
-        if (tag_id != ECMA_ExtendedFileEntry) {
+        if (tag_id == ECMA_ExtendedFileEntry) {
+            fe = decode_ext_file_entry(buf, UDF_BLOCK_SIZE, pd->number);
+        } else if (tag_id == ECMA_FileEntry) {
+            fe = decode_file_entry(buf, UDF_BLOCK_SIZE, pd->number);
+        } else {
             udf_error("read metadata file %u: unexpected tag %d\n", i, tag_id);
             continue;
         }
-
-        fe = decode_ext_file_entry(buf, UDF_BLOCK_SIZE, pd->number);
         if (!fe) {
             udf_error("parsing metadata file entry %u failed\n", i);
             continue;
